@startuml agent-exe-anatomy
title The agent AS the product — what "HR Desk Setup.exe" installs

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #888888
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

package "Installed product: «HR Desk»   (the user never sees the word agentd)" as PROD #F0FFF0 {

  rectangle "HR Desk.exe — the SHELL\n--\nONE shared Electron shell codebase,\nbranded per agent by FLAVOR (config, not forks).\nIts only jobs:\n1. find-or-start the daemon (supervisor)\n2. first run: install the bundled .agentpkg\n3. open ONE window → /apps/hr-desk/\n\nNO JARVIS renderer in this experience —\nthe agent's own ui/ IS the product" as SHELL

  file "distribution.toml\n--\n[product]\nid · name · icon\napp_agent = 'hr-desk'   «the knob»\npreinstalled_bundles = [...]" as DIST

  folder "resources/python\n--\nrelocatable CPython + agentd\nTHE full engine: gateway, tools,\nplugins, marketplace — SAME bytes\nthe agentd desktop app ships" as RT

  file "bundles/hr-desk.agentpkg\n--\nthe AGENT, whole:\nagent.toml ([app] title/mode) · IDENTITY.md\nui/ (the custom app UI, by its author)\nplugins/ (agent-private tools)\nskills/ · templates/" as PKG
}

package "shared per-user machine state  (owned by the DAEMON, not by any product)" as STATE #EAF3FF {
  file "~/.agentd/gateway.json\nrendezvous: {host, port, pid, token}\n= how every product finds\nthe ONE daemon" as RDV
  folder "agents/<id>/…  +  <state_dir>/…\ninstalled agents · sessions ·\nmemory · workspaces" as ROOT
}

SHELL -down-> DIST : reads at boot
SHELL -down-> RT : spawns the daemon from\n(only if none is running)
SHELL -down-> PKG : installs on first run\n(marketplace.install RPC)
SHELL -right-> RDV : find-or-start
PKG .down.> ROOT : unpacked into\nagents/hr-desk/

note bottom of PROD
  ZERO backend changes: the shell only CONSUMES the daemon's published
  protocol (supervisor + marketplace.install + /apps serving + scope).
  The invariant holds even for an exe: an agent app may INVOKE the
  backend in new ways, never extend it.
end note
@enduml

@startuml agent-exe-launch
title Double-click → using the agent — all four install cases in one flow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #888888
  ParticipantBackgroundColor White
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

actor "User A\n(knows only «HR Desk»)" as U
participant "HR Desk.exe\n(shell main process)" as SH
participant "Supervisor" as SUP
participant "~/.agentd/gateway.json\n(rendezvous)" as RDV
participant "agentd daemon\n(the engine)" as D
participant "App window\n/apps/hr-desk/" as W

U -> SH : double-click
SH -> SH : load flavor: distribution.toml\n→ app_agent = "hr-desk"
SH -> SUP : ensure()
SUP -> RDV : read + liveness check
alt a daemon is ALREADY running   (case 4: agentd desktop or another agent exe put it there)
  RDV --> SUP : {host, port, token} — reuse it
else no daemon on this machine   (cases 1–3: this exe is the ONLY thing installed)
  SUP -> D : spawn from the EMBEDDED runtime\n(resources/python — ships in this exe)
  D -> RDV : write {host, port, pid, token}
end
SH -> D : marketplace.installed   (WS, stable protocol)
alt "hr-desk" not installed yet   (first launch of this product)
  SH -> D : marketplace.install {file: bundles/hr-desk.agentpkg}
  D -> D : unpack → agents/hr-desk/\nhot-load its private plugins\n(no restart)
end
SH -> W : BrowserWindow →\nhttp://host:port/apps/hr-desk/?token=…&scope=agent:hr-desk
W -> D : WebSocket (scoped to agent:hr-desk)\nchat.send · tools.invoke · events
D --> W : chat.event stream · artifacts via /file
U -> W : works with HR Desk —\nnever saw agentd, never opened another app

note over SH, D
  Splash while the daemon cold-starts (seconds, first time only).
  Later launches: rendezvous hits a live daemon → window is instant.
end note
@enduml

@startuml agent-exe-pipeline
title From an agent folder to an installed product — and how products COEXIST

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #888888
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

package "AUTHOR side — build pipeline (per agent = one build parameter, zero new code)" as BUILD #FDF6FF {
  folder "agents/hr-desk/\nagent.toml ([app] mode) · ui/ ·\nplugins/ · skills/" as SRC
  rectangle "agentd bundle pack\n→ hr-desk.agentpkg" as PACK
  rectangle "flavor generator (script)\n→ flavors/hr-desk/\ndistribution.toml (app_agent) ·\nbundles/ · icon" as GEN
  rectangle "electron-builder\n(ONE generic app-shell config)\n+ embedded runtime" as EB
  rectangle "«HR Desk Setup.exe»\n(NSIS, per-user install)\nDELIVERED INTO the agent's own\nagents/hr-desk/clients/desktop/\n(excluded from packing + git —\nderived, never source)" as EXE
  rectangle "marketplace (web)\n[ Install ] ← what User A clicks\n(cloud registry — later phase)" as MKT
}

SRC -right-> PACK
PACK -right-> GEN
GEN -right-> EB
EB -right-> EXE
EXE -down-> MKT : uploaded / served

package "USER machine — many products, ONE engine" as MACH #F0FFF0 {
  rectangle "HR Desk.exe\n(window → /apps/hr-desk/)" as P1
  rectangle "Figure Studio.exe\n(window → /apps/figure-creator/)" as P2
  rectangle "agentd desktop (JARVIS)\n(the full generalist UI —\noptional, NOT required)" as P3
  rectangle "ONE agentd daemon  :8787\nfound via ~/.agentd/gateway.json\nfirst product to launch starts it;\nevery later one reuses it" as ONE #EAF3FF
  folder "one shared state root\nagents/ · sessions/ · memory/\n(HR Desk shows up in JARVIS's\nagent list — same agent!)" as SR
}

MKT .down.> P1 : User A installs
P1 -down-> ONE
P2 -down-> ONE
P3 -down-> ONE
ONE -right-> SR

note bottom of MACH
  Uninstalling a product removes ITS shell only; the daemon + state stay
  while anything else uses them. Installing the full agentd desktop later
  reveals every agent-exe's agent already there — products COMPOSE,
  because there is exactly one engine and one state root per machine.
end note
@enduml
